    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n11200" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπαγρι-όομαι</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>become wild</i> or <i>savage,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μή μ᾽ ἐκπλαγῆτ᾽ . . ἀπηγριωμένον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Ph.</u>
					226
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Plt.</u>
				274b
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπὸ τῶν στατήρων ἦν
				ἀπηγριωμένη</span> had been <i>made saucy</i> by riches,
				<i><span class="en">
				Epicr.
				3.16
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> of plants,
				<i>revert to wild state,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Thphr.
				<u>HP</u>
				2.2.9
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				3.2.2
			</span></i>.</div>
